## Stack

Bun · Hono · `@hono/zod-openapi` (OpenAPI-first routing) · Scalar · Drizzle ORM · PostgreSQL
Better Auth · BullMQ · Redis (ioredis) · S3-compatible object storage
Pino · Sentry · `<third-party clients — one per external provider>`

## Architecture

Modular monolith — feature verticals with internal layering. `src/modules/<reference-module>/` is
the reference module; `AGENTS.md` "How to Add a New Module" is the pattern every module follows.
Folders hold files or folders, never both (`.claude/rules/common/folder-shape.md`).

```
src/
  index.ts             bootstrap only — imports env.ts first, mounts the API docs and
                       /openapi.json, starts the server and the workers
  app.ts               composition only — middleware, onError/notFound, app.route() mounts.
                       Middleware order is fixed by AGENTS.md §I Rule 41
  env.ts               Zod env schema; the only file that reads process.env; exits on a bad value
  lib/
    server/            factory.ts (createRouter, AppEnv), logger.ts (Pino)
    errors/            errors.ts (the DomainError hierarchy), problem.ts (the RFC 9457 mapper,
                       the 422 defaultHook, the 404 handler), error-codes.ts (ERROR_CODES)
    constants/         the one home of every shared identifier (AGENTS.md Rule 43)
    auth/              auth.ts — better-auth configuration
    <client>/          one folder per service client (redis, storage, each provider); no
                       business logic
  db/
    client/            index.ts — the real connection pool; migrate.ts — the single-connection
                       migration runner
    schema/            Drizzle schema, one file per domain; auth.ts is generated by the
                       better-auth CLI
    migrations/        drizzle-kit output. Never hand-edited
  middlewares/         logger, rate-limit (/api/* only), auth guards
  modules/<name>/      routes, handler, service, schema, errors, index, __tests__/, and a
                       repository only on escalation (AGENTS.md Rule 4)
  queues/              BullMQ queues and their workers
  test/                config.ts (the integration-tier gate), preload.ts (the shared doubles)
```

`<State each deliberate absence in one sentence: "there is no repository layer in <module>; its
service queries the db directly, which Rule 4 allows" stops the next audit from reporting it.>`

## Authentication

better-auth, configured in `src/lib/auth/auth.ts`. `<Name the decisions that carry the posture,
each commented at its definition: how accounts are created, which sign-in methods exist, whether a
second factor is required, and the session lifetimes.>`

Sessions live in Redis (`secondaryStorage`) when it is configured; the Postgres `session` table is
then a mirror. End sessions through better-auth, never with a row delete
(`.claude/anti-patterns/session-rows-are-a-mirror-not-the-session.md`).

## Error Contract — RFC 9457

Every thrown error becomes `application/problem+json`: `{ type, title, status, detail, instance,
code }`, plus `requestId`, and `fields` on a 422. `app.onError` (`handleAppError` in
`src/lib/errors/problem.ts`, wired in `src/app.ts`) is the single mapper for `DomainError`
subclasses, Hono `HTTPException` and unknown errors; `app.notFound` gives unmatched routes the same
shape. Schema validation failures return `422`. Every code is listed once in
`src/lib/errors/error-codes.ts`. Rules: `AGENTS.md` §C and `.claude/rules/common/error-codes.md`.

## Database

- `src/db/client/index.ts` holds the real connection pool, explicitly configured (AGENTS.md §I
  Rule 38): `max` (`DB_POOL_MAX`), `idle_timeout`, `connect_timeout`, `max_lifetime`, `prepare`
  (`DB_PREPARE`), plus `connection.statement_timeout` and
  `idle_in_transaction_session_timeout`.
- `src/db/client/migrate.ts` uses its own single-connection client (`{ max: 1 }`) — correct there,
  wrong everywhere else (`.claude/anti-patterns/postgres-max-1-pool.md`).
- `src/db/schema/` holds `<list each schema file and the tables it owns>`. Migrations
  (`bun run db:generate`) are committed in the same PR as the schema change;
  `scripts/check/migrations.sh` enforces it in CI.
- Query rules are AGENTS.md §H; the deeper reference is `.claude/rules/backend/drizzle.md`.
  Agent access through the `db-dev`/`db-prod` MCP servers is described in `.claude/DATABASE.md`.

## Testing

Two tiers, both on Bun's built-in runner (`bunfig.toml` scopes discovery to `src/`):

- **Unit** — `bun test src` (`bun run test`). No database, Redis or network:
  `src/test/preload.ts` replaces every external client for the whole run. The quality gate runs
  this tier, with coverage.
- **Integration** — `bun run test:integration` (`RUN_INTEGRATION_TESTS=1 bun test src`):
  `*.integration.test.ts` files gated by `shouldRunIntegrationTests()`, against Postgres 17 and
  Redis 7 (`docker compose up -d`).

Coverage (`bun run test:coverage`) is 100% per file, lines and functions, over all of `src/**`,
and `scripts/check/coverage-files.mjs` fails on any source file no test loads. The exemptions in
`bunfig.toml` are a closed list; the policy is `.claude/rules/typescript/coverage.md`.

## Pipeline

Every workflow starts from a pull-request event; nothing runs on a push or a schedule.

- **Pre-commit** (`.husky/pre-commit` running `scripts/check/gates.sh --hook`) — the gates in
  `scripts/check/gates.list` that the staged files need, before every commit.
- **Quality gate** (`.github/workflows/quality-gate.yml`, calling agent-config-kit's
  `be-hono-quality-gate` workflow) — every pull request.
- **Read-only checks** (`workflows-lint.yml`, `dependency-review.yml`, `codeql.yml`) — every pull
  request (workflows-lint only when `.github/` changes).
- **Deploy** — `<the workflow that deploys, and the event that starts it (for example a pull
  request merged into prod)>`
- **AI-layer strip** — `<if the deployed branch drops .claude/, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and
  SSOT.md, the workflow that does it; otherwise delete this line>`

If the strip runs, what a person needs after it lives in `README.md`, not here: this file does
not survive on `prod`.

## Env Variables

```
NODE_ENV · PORT
DATABASE_URL             postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/db   (required)
REDIS_URL                redis://host:6379/<db-index>           (required)
CORS_ORIGINS             comma-separated allowlist, e.g. https://<app-host>.
                         A missing value falls back to the schema default and blocks every
                         browser call from the real frontend origin — an outage no health check
                         reports. Always set it explicitly.
DB_POOL_MAX              max Postgres pool size (production: 10)
DB_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS  default 10000 — below the request timeout
DB_PREPARE               true | false — false behind a transaction-mode pooler
REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS       default 15000
BODY_LIMIT_BYTES         default 1048576 (1 MiB)
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET       min 32 chars
BETTER_AUTH_URL          this API's own origin, e.g. https://api-<app-host>
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID · GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
<PROVIDER>_API_KEY       one line per third-party client, with its format hint
S3_ENDPOINT · S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID · S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY · S3_BUCKET_NAME
SENTRY_DSN               optional
```

No other environment variables are read anywhere in `src/`. If you add one, update `src/env.ts`'s
Zod schema, `.env.<target>.example`, and this list in the same PR.

`<A variable an agent would assume exists, and why it does not>` — state the negatives here too.
"`<SERVICE>_URL` does not exist in this repo's environment — this repo never calls that service"
stops the assumption at the source, the same way §Ecosystem does for the arrows.

## Branches

```
internal/{scope} → dev (quality gate on the PR) → prod (quality gate on the promotion PR, then the
                                                         deploy)
```

Naming: `internal/{scope}` for a single task; `internal/{scope}/{context}` for parallel tasks
sharing a scope. Never push directly to `dev` or `prod`.

## Known traps

`<A behaviour of a dependency or the platform that looks like a bug in this repo's code: what it
does, how it was proven, and the workaround in place. Once it has a root cause and a fix, move it to
.claude/anti-patterns/ and leave a one-line pointer here.>`

A known one to check on your versions: `z.infer` of a schema built with `z` from
`@hono/zod-openapi`, and `c.req.valid(...)`, can resolve to `any` when the package's `zod` and the
repo's own `zod` differ. Nothing fails; the types simply stop checking. Hover one before trusting it,
and until the versions agree, declare the service's input types by hand.

## Transactional email

`<Fill in once the service sends mail.>` The shape that holds:

- **One guarded send path**: every message goes through one function that checks the quota and logs
  the recipient hashed, never the address or the body.
- **Synchronous for mail a person is waiting on** (a sign-in code); queued for the rest. A job
  carries the data to render, never rendered HTML, so a template fix reaches mail already queued.
- **One locale resolver and typed message catalogues**, shared with the web copy.
- **A refused send is not retried** when the quota counter moves before it compares: a retry would
  spend the quota again.
